{"id":53692558339894,"type":"genre","name":"experimental","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":63,"info":{"img":null},"own_scenes":[],"similar_scenes":[{"id":14645526142621,"name":"Experimental alemán: Einstürzende Neubauten","book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","start":1979,"end":1993,"desc":"En Alemania, ruido y anarquía más allá del industrial, entre la estética punk y el expresionismo: Der Plan, Die Krupps, P16D4, Die Haut, HNAS y, sobre todo, Einstürzende Neubauten, teatro vivo de la autodestrucción con objetos encontrados y cadencias industriales (Kollaps, Zeichnungen des Patienten OT), más cercanos a Beckett que a Chuck Berry. DAF, Palais Schaumburg y Xmal Deutschland llevan el synth-pop hacia el baile industrial; Malaria, Yello, Die Form (Francia), Maurizio Bianchi (Italia) y Esplendor Geométrico (España).","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Gótico e industrial","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#german-noise"},{"id":104673682705698,"name":"Pop experimental de Sheffield","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1974,"end":1990,"desc":"Cabaret Voltaire (1974) hacía «música pop experimental»: menos apocalípticos que TG, influidos por Seeds, la Velvet y Warhol y, caso raro, por el dub. Su industrial fue el puente entre el pop y el house y el techno, que a su vez les influyeron: acabaron grabando con Marshall Jefferson en Chicago.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Industrial y ruido","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#sheffield"},{"id":276388115832069,"name":"Leftfield (electrónica experimental post-rave)","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1990,"end":2002,"desc":"La experimental de los noventa fue post-rave y post-digital: veteranos del industrial y desertores del techno ensanchan la tierra de nadie entre lo culto y lo popular, donde conviven dance, noise, drones, ambient, improvisación, electroacústica y computer music. La prensa lo llamó «leftfield»: no un sonido, sino una perspectiva heterodoxa capaz de apreciar a la vez a Gottfried Michael Koenig, los dubs de King Tubby y la marcialidad de Surgeon. Psychic TV, Chris & Cosey y Coil abrazan el acid.","color":"#8b7cf6","family":"Vanguardia y experimental","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#leftfield"},{"id":249139167499570,"name":"Experimental vs. techno","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":2000,"end":2010,"desc":"Los artistas de la escena post-digital de los noventa regresan al techno y al ambient: técnicas difíciles con resultados de club.","color":"#22d3ee","family":"Techno y derivados","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#experimental-techno"}],"aka":[],"rym":[],"artists":[{"id":131837656417857,"type":"artist","name":"David Bowie","artist":null,"year":1947,"weight":3553,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":132878248289584,"type":"artist","name":"The Velvet Underground","artist":null,"year":1964,"weight":973,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":158197663535109,"type":"artist","name":"Bjork","artist":null,"year":1965,"weight":777,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":156479957595892,"type":"artist","name":"Kraftwerk","artist":null,"year":1970,"weight":688,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":269588055362758,"type":"artist","name":"The Pixies","artist":null,"year":1986,"weight":478,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":64209384530380,"type":"artist","name":"John Frusciante","artist":null,"year":1970,"weight":397,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":188548856103507,"type":"artist","name":"Swans","artist":null,"year":1982,"weight":267,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":175070559046094,"type":"artist","name":"The KLF","artist":null,"year":1988,"weight":157,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":250376165540155,"type":"artist","name":"The Residents","artist":null,"year":1966,"weight":142,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"},{"id":35883852588104,"type":"